# A Notion Thief on each side: "if each player in a two-player game controls a Notion Thief and one would draw a card, it
# really will be that player who draws a card" (its ruling; CR 614.5, 616.1). Bot2 casts Ancestral Recall: each draw is
# replaced by Bot1's Notion Thief (Bot2's own does not replace its controller's draws), so Bot1 would draw instead; that draw
# is an opponent's of Bot2, outside its draw step, so Bot2's Notion Thief replaces it, and Bot2 would draw; Bot1's Notion
# Thief has had its one opportunity at that draw already, so Bot2 draws the card. Bot2 draws all three, Bot1 none - and
# nothing goes round for ever.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Notion Thief
Swamp x4
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Notion Thief
Mox Sapphire
Ancestral Recall
Swamp x2
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Notion Thief.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Hand.Count = 8
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Notion Thief.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot2)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 4
Bot1.Library.Count = 20
Bot2.Hand.Count = 6
Bot2.Library.Count = 16
